rmnet_shs: softnet_data.dropped became the per-NUMA drop_counters on 6.18

rmnet_shs_drop_backlog() counts the backlog skbs it frees as softnet drops, as
enqueue_to_backlog() does; 6.18 replaced atomic_t sd->dropped with struct
numa_drop_counters drop_counters (numa_drop_add(), read back by /proc/net/softnet_stat).

--- a/drivers612/conn/data/src/datarmnet-ext/shs/rmnet_shs_main.c
+++ b/drivers612/conn/data/src/datarmnet-ext/shs/rmnet_shs_main.c
@@ -1594,7 +1594,8 @@
 			dev_core_stats_rx_dropped_inc(skb->dev);
 #if (KERNEL_VERSION(6, 9, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE)
 			rps_input_queue_head_incr(sd);
-			atomic_inc(&sd->dropped);
+			/* 6.18: softnet_data.dropped became drop_counters (as enqueue_to_backlog) */
+			numa_drop_add(&sd->drop_counters, 1);
 #else
 			input_queue_head_incr(sd);
 			sd->dropped++;
